{"type":"standard","title":"Hasha language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Hasha language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3915338","titles":{"canonical":"Hasha_language","normalized":"Hasha language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Hasha language</span></span>"},"pageid":33468489,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1139886963","tid":"4268e2fc-aeb0-11ed-82e2-d8add780dd89","timestamp":"2023-02-17T10:45:57Z","description":"Plateau language spoken in Nigeria","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasha_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasha_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasha_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Hasha_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasha_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Hasha_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasha_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Hasha_language"}},"extract":"Hasha, also known as Yashi, is a Plateau language of Nasarawa State Nigeria. It has an idiosyncratic system of reduplicating the first syllable of noun stems, apparently under the influence of the Chadic language Sha.","extract_html":"<p><b>Hasha</b>, also known as <i>Yashi</i>, is a Plateau language of Nasarawa State Nigeria. It has an idiosyncratic system of reduplicating the first syllable of noun stems, apparently under the influence of the Chadic language Sha.</p>"}